{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on E1 question `2e6f4bd8`: confirmed.\n\n1. While an output is pending, a reached lookup by a number that\n   names no recorded item answers `unavailable`, and it lacks `entry`.\n   The pending output can receive that number, so absence is not\n   known.\n2. A number that names a recorded item reads its hypothetical content.\n3. A named pending source resolves by its token.\n4. With no pending output, ordinary absence stays unchanged, and the\n   recorded answers stay identical.\n\nThis is item 3 of `1bdf9467` applied to a lookup. It adds no validator\nchange, no allocation rule and no second evaluator. One test covers\neach of the four cases.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2e6f4bd873c5c975fdfcb72ecc68d0b77cbb370a stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:02c1227e7dc1c04a96ab423dd34c58537b63a2f2, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:03c2d3b4bab05912804bc48129712cd98f805758, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:06d96cd732ff547fa8959619d6df87c5953f2ded, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0d76705dfdd74d8de0047a7a257da83b75d575e2 and 73 more","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}